course: dictionary
lesson: 2068
title: Consonants: the letters that are not vowels
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A consonant is a letter that is not a vowel. The five vowels are a, e, i, o and u, so the other letters of the alphabet are consonants, such as b, c, d, f and g. Y can be either: it is a consonant at the start of «yes» but works like a vowel in «happy».
explain: A consonant can also be a speech sound. You make it by partly blocking the air with your lips, tongue or teeth. Say «b» and feel your lips close, then open. Say «s» and feel your tongue touch your teeth. Those are both consonant sounds.
explain: The word consonant also has a formal meaning. When two things are consonant with each other, they are in agreement. «Her plan is consonant with ours» means her plan agrees with ours.
fact: A consonant is a letter that is not a vowel.
fact: English has 21 consonant letters and 5 vowels: a, e, i, o and u.
fact: «Consonant + y changes to i before -ed» so «cry» becomes «cried», but «crying» keeps the y.
fact: In «running», the n is doubled because «run» has one short vowel and one final consonant.
fact: «Consonant with» is a formal phrase that means in agreement with.
exercise: Which of these letters is a consonant? | e | a | i | *b
exercise: «Consonant + y changes to i before -ed (cry, cried) but keeps the y before -ing (crying).» What happens to the y in «crying»? | It becomes e | *It stays as y | It is removed | It becomes i
exercise: «Her plan is consonant with ours.» What does consonant with mean here? | *In agreement with | Broken into pieces | Far away from | Very loud
test: Which word has a double consonant? | tree | hat | *hopping | sun
test: How many consonant letters does English have? | 5 | *21 | 12 | 26
exam: In «yes», the y is at the start of the word. What kind of sound does it make? | A vowel sound, like /ie/ in «my» | *A consonant sound | A double vowel sound | A silent sound
